ashy bars I  like that it's a it's an MIT dive bar  and there were these geeky and mighty  kids who used to hang out there and they  were your regular math science kids  except for strangely enough they had  tons of money and it was always in  hundred-dollar bills and in Boston you  never see a hundred dollar bill you know  in New York you see hundred dollar bills  you know in in Vegas you see they come  out of the ATM machines right but in  Boston the last time I saw a hundred  dollar bill I don't can't even remember  so I went over to this kid and I said  why do you have so much money and he  invites me to his house so I go over  this kid's house and he points to his  laundry and stacked above his laundry  it's two hundred and fifty thousand  dollars and hundreds in banded stacks  and I'm like okay this guy's a drug  dealer but you know I didn't look like a  drug dealer and he said no no I'm not a  drug dealer  come to Vegas and the next day I flew to  Vegas because I was in that part of my  life and I landed in Vegas and six of  his friends flew with us and they all  get out and we all they pretended they  didn't know each other and we go to this  suite it was like a suite overlooking  the hall the whole strip and the kids  start to pull money out from under their  clothes and they had a million dollars  in cash that they had flown from Boston  to Vegas with and they pile it up on the  table and they say we're the mit  blackjack team and I was blown away and  I realized you know I'm gonna become a  nonfiction writer because this is the  craziest thing I've ever seen and I  joined the team and I played with them  for about six months and and you know it  was a crazy experience being like the  donkey boy if any of you saw the movie  21 I was the guy who strapped a quarter  million dollars to my body and did all  that stuff and it was intense and then  it got more intense because Kevin Spacey  called me about  week before the book came out and  somehow he had gotten